Package: debiasforest
Title: Bias Correction for Random Forest Regression
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("John", "Ryan", email = "jpryan7@wisc.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Bias-correction methods for random forest regression compared in
    Chen, Withana Gamage and Ryan (2022) <doi:10.3329/jsr.v56i2.67466>: the
    boosted forest (forests fitted to out-of-bag residuals), univariate
    smoothing of the out-of-bag predictions (linear, quadratic, cubic and
    smoothing spline) and the conditional bias correction of Lu and Hardin
    (2021). Built on 'randomForest' forests, with the paper's simulation
    designs, a stopping rule for the number of boosting iterations and helpers
    for simulation studies and repeated train/test splits.
